OL,3,AEmployers should teach primary-age
OL,4,Achildren about work, says Milburn
OL,5,
OL,6,FChildren should be introduced to the
OL,7,Fworld of work at the start of primary
OL,8,Fschool, says the author of a major
OL,9,Freport into youth activity in the UK.
OL,11,FFormer minister Alan Milburn says
OL,12,Fchildren as young as four should be
OL,13,Flearning about different careers, with
OL,14,Fwork experience placements made
OL,15,Fmandatory for 14- to 16-year-olds.
OL,17,FHowever, teaching unions warn of the
OL,18,F"significant pressure" already facing
OL,19,Fprimary schools and say practical
OL,20,Fconsiderations must ensure all schools
OL,21,Fhave access to the support.
OL,23,APub: 30-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/38
